From: festevam@gmail.com (Fabio Estevam)
Date: Sat, 24 Mar 2018 11:55:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dma-mapping: Use vma_pages()
Message-ID: <1521903319-2977-1-git-send-email-festevam@gmail.com>
To: linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
List-Id: linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org

From: Fabio Estevam <fabio.estevam@nxp.com>

Use vma_pages() function instead of open coding it.

Generated by scripts/coccinelle/api/vma_pages.cocci.

Signed-off-by: Fabio Estevam <fabio.estevam@nxp.com>
---
 arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c b/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c
index 8c398fe..c25cca6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c
@@ -845,7 +845,7 @@ static int __arm_dma_mmap(struct device *dev, struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 		 unsigned long attrs)
 {
 	int ret;
-	unsigned long nr_vma_pages = (vma->vm_end - vma->vm_start) >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+	unsigned long nr_vma_pages = vma_pages(vma);
 	unsigned long nr_pages = PAGE_ALIGN(size) >> PAGE_SHIFT;
 	unsigned long pfn = dma_to_pfn(dev, dma_addr);
 	unsigned long off = vma->vm_pgoff;
-- 
2.7.4
